title: Responsible Use of Generative AI in Assisted Coding - CodeRefinery lesson
type: dataset
abstract: 'A CodeRefinery lesson providing a practical framework for researchers who
  want to use AI coding assistants responsibly. The lesson covers three scenarios
  of increasing automation (chat-based coding, IDE integration, and agentic coding),
  security considerations including hallucinated packages and prompt injection, and
  mitigation strategies. Includes a hands-on workshop on data exploration and visualisation
  with Python and generative AI.

  '
